<title>PERU: Nestle sees Peruvian buy &quot;very close&quot;.</title>
<headline>Nestle sees Peruvian buy &quot;very close&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's Nestle SA said Friday it was close to finalizing the purchase of Peru's largest ice-cream and confectionery company D'Onofrio.</p>
<p>&quot;We are getting very close. It is probable that the deal will be finished shortly, but of course anything can happen,&quot; said Nestle's spokesman in Peru, Edgar Sanchez.</p>
<p>Nestle has previously said that if it is not successful in its bid to buy D'Onofrio, it would import ice creams to Peru from plants owned by its subsidiaries in Chile, Argentina and Venezuela.</p>
<p>The company would not give financial details of its negotiations with D'Onofrio.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
